          "title": "Tell HN: OpenAI now requires ID verification and won't refund API credits",
          "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=45702363",
          "source": "Hacker News",
          "date": "2025-10-25T09:02:14Z",
          "language": "en",
          "section": "us_news",
          "raw_content": "Just frustrated here: I credited my OpenAI API account with credits, and then it turns out I have to go through some verification process to actually use the API, which involves disclosing personal data to some third-party vendor, which I am not prepared to do. So I asked for a refund and am told that that refunds are against their policy. So I'll be cancelling my chatgpt plus sub, disputing the card payment, and moving to deepseek. Edit: Deepseek seems to be a lot cheaper than OpenAI Edit 2: seems verification is only needed for gpt-5, gpt-4o seems to work without it",
